Usage: nimbu <command> [flags]

CLI for the Nimbu API - AI-agent first, human-friendly second

Getting started:
  auth                    Authentication and credentials
  init                    Bootstrap a local theme project
  sites                   Manage sites
  server                  Run local simulator proxy with child dev server
  env                     Manage project environments
  config                  Manage configuration

Content:
  channels                Manage channels and entries
  pages                   Manage pages
  menus                   Manage navigation menus
  mails (mail)            Sync notification templates to local files
  notifications           Manage notifications
  uploads                 Manage uploads
  blogs                   Manage blogs
  translations            Manage translations

Commerce:
  products                Manage products
  shipping-rates          Manage shipping rates
  collections             Manage collections
  coupons                 Manage coupons
  orders                  Manage orders
  customers               Manage customers

Theme & code:
  schema                  Manage declarative schemas
  release                 Release schema, cloud code and theme
  releases                List successful releases
  functions               Execute cloud functions
  jobs                    Execute cloud jobs
  apps                    Manage OAuth apps
  themes                  Manage themes

Admin:
  domains                 Manage custom domains
  announcements           Manage platform announcements
  domain-registrations    Manage domain registrations
  settings                Manage site settings
  events                  Track and ingest events
  realtime                Realtime grants and live queries
  roles                   Manage roles
  redirects               Manage redirects
  senders                 Manage email sender domains
  webhooks                Manage webhooks

Advanced:
  api                     Raw API access
  commands                Export the machine-readable command contract
  completion              Generate shell completions

Global Flags:
  -h, --help           Show context-sensitive help.
      --env=STRING     Named project environment (overrides site and API URL)
      --site=STRING    Site ID or subdomain, else nimbu.yml site ($NIMBU_SITE)
      --json           Output JSON to stdout ($NIMBU_JSON)
      --plain          Output stable TSV to stdout ($NIMBU_PLAIN)
      --verbose        Enable verbose logging
      --debug          Enable debug logging (HTTP traces)
      --version        Print version and exit

Examples:
  # Log in, then list the sites you can access
  nimbu auth login
  nimbu sites list

  # Bootstrap a theme project and run the local dev server
  nimbu init my-theme
  nimbu server

  # List the entries of a channel as JSON
  nimbu channels entries list --channel blog --json

  # Update an entry with inline assignments
  nimbu channels entries update --channel blog --entry welcome title=Welcome

Run "nimbu help <command>" for more information on a command.
Create/Update supports inline payloads using: key=value, key:=json,
key=@file.txt or key:=@file.json
Run "nimbu --help-all" for all flags.
